================================================================================
WHAT THE MIT GRANT ABOVE DOES AND DOES NOT COVER
================================================================================

It covers the work original to this repository: train/script/, eval/, docs/,
the configs, and the plate-specific additions. It does not and cannot cover
third-party code and weights redistributed here under their own terms, listed
below. Where they conflict, theirs govern.

synth/ -- GPL
    synth/tw/Synthtext/ and synth/cn/Synthtext/ derive from SRNet-Datagen,
    Copyright (c) 2019 Netease Youdao Information Technology Co., Ltd., written
    by Yu Qian, released under the GPL. Twelve files carry that header. GPL is
    copyleft: derivatives must also be GPL and ship their source. It is not
    compatible with relicensing under MIT, so those files keep their own terms
    and the MIT grant above does not extend to them. They are a standalone data
    generation tool -- nothing under src/ imports them at runtime -- but if you
    redistribute a modified synth/, GPL applies to what you ship.

src/ -- upstream licence unstated
    src/ derives from FLUX-Text (https://github.com/AMAP-ML/FluxText), which as
    of this writing publishes no LICENSE file and states no terms. Code with no
    stated licence grants no rights by default. This is the upstream project's
    gap, not something this repository can resolve; treat src/ as usable for
    research and seek permission from its authors before anything else.

Released model weights -- FLUX.1 [dev] Non-Commercial License
    Every adapter released alongside this repository is a LoRA over
    FLUX.1-Fill-dev, distributed by Black Forest Labs under the FLUX.1 [dev]
    Non-Commercial License. That licence governs the base weights, the adapters
    derived from them, and images generated with either. odm_epoch_100.pt comes
    from FLUX-Text; the TRBA recognisers derive from
    deep-text-recognition-benchmark (Clova AI, Apache-2.0); the DeepSolo++
    detector keeps its own terms.

Fonts and data
    TWGen7_V1.ttf, CCDP_TEXT0620.ttf and 正黑體.ttf are third-party typefaces
    redistributed for research reproduction; see font/README.md. SynthText
    backgrounds are downloaded from their authors, not redistributed. CCPD2019
    and LP-2025 keep their publishers' terms.

If you intend to use any of this commercially, resolve the FLUX.1 [dev]
non-commercial restriction and the src/ licensing gap first. This file is a
description of what is here, not legal advice.
